course: dictionary
lesson: 607
title: Awful: one word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Awful is a strong word, and its main meaning is very bad or unpleasant. But it can also mean that you feel ill, very unhappy or guilty. «He lies awake feeling awful and says sorry at breakfast.» Here the words feeling and sorry tell you he feels bad inside, not that the weather or a smell is bad.
explain: «Saying "I was wrong" in front of everyone felt awful for about ten seconds.» The clue is for about ten seconds: the bad feeling was short, and it was an embarrassed, uncomfortable feeling. Always ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Look at the words around awful. «An awful lot» is informal and means a very large amount, so it is not bad at all. Your clues are the words before and after it, like an and lot.
explain: In writing, teachers may ask you to swap awful for a more exact word, such as terrible, dreadful, horrid or disgusting. Choose the one that fits the sentence best.
fact: Awful means very bad or unpleasant, as in awful weather or an awful smell.
fact: If you feel awful, you feel ill, very unhappy or guilty.
fact: «An awful lot» is an informal phrase that means a very large amount.
fact: Long ago, awful meant full of awe: very impressive and frightening.
fact: In writing, terrible, dreadful, horrid and disgusting can often replace awful to make your meaning more exact.
exercise: «He lies awake feeling awful and says sorry at breakfast.» How does he feel? | Excited about the party | Hungry for toast | Very rich | *Ill, very unhappy or guilty
exercise: «Saying "I was wrong" in front of everyone felt awful for about ten seconds.» What does felt awful show? | Everyone was asleep | *It was an uncomfortable, embarrassed feeling | It was the best day ever | Our teacher gave a long, boring lesson
exercise: Jayden says, «I have an awful lot of homework.» What does an awful lot mean? | A very bad amount | Not enough at all | A small, tidy pile | *A very large amount
test: In a writing lesson, which word is a more exact replacement for awful? | Sleepy | *Terrible | Happy | Tiny
test: «The fines were simply awful.» Which meaning fits best? | Very kind and helpful | Very quiet and gentle | Very cheap and easy to pay | *Very bad or unpleasant
exam: «He felt awful after breaking the window.» Which meaning of awful fits best here? | A very large number of windows | Full of awe and very impressive | Very tall and wide | *Ill, unhappy or guilty
